<title>USA: Midwest Express votes three-for-two split.</title>
<headline>Midwest Express votes three-for-two split.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Midwest Express Holdings Inc said Wednesday its board approved a plan to split its stock three-for-two in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend.</p>
<p>On May 28, shareholders will get one additional share of common stock for every two they hold on May 12, the record date.  </p>
<p>Midwest Express has about 6.4 million shares outstanding. The split wil increase the number to about 9.6 million.</p>
<p>The split comes 19 months after the airline holding company became publicly held.</p>
<p>	  ((Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
